# Push to main for Vercel after updates

After finishing user-requested work that changes the app or docs, **commit and push to `main`** so Vercel redeploys and phone/browser testing stays current.

## Always push when you change

- `src/**`, `public/**` (except see feature flags note below)
- `index.html`, `vite.config.*`, `package.json` / lockfile when needed for the change
- `docs/ui-snapshots/**`, `docs/confluence-weekly-build-in-public.md`, `docs/confluence-attachments/**`
- Snapshot / Confluence scripts under `scripts/`

## Workflow

1. Finish the requested change.
2. `git add` relevant paths (never `.env` or secrets).
3. Commit with a clear message.
4. `git pull --rebase origin main` if remote is ahead.
5. `git push origin main`.
6. Tell the user the live URL if relevant: https://ncaaf-data-collection.vercel.app

Do not leave finished UI/app work only on disk.

## Snapshots / Confluence

After `capture:*`, `sync:confluence-doc`, or `publish:confluence`, also commit and push the generated docs/snapshot paths as above.

## Exception — feature flag defaults

`public/feature-flag-defaults.json` only ships via **Confirm & deploy** in the app unless the user explicitly asks to commit those defaults. You may still add new flag keys with safe defaults when introducing a flag.
